---
/* ============================================================
   Preface — the author's note before a piece of writing: where it
   came from, why it is here. It keeps the post's own body face but
   runs a step quieter (muted), so the piece that follows reads as the
   main voice.

     <Preface>

     I recently took a storytelling workshop. …

     </Preface>

   Leave a blank line inside each tag so the paragraphs stay Markdown.
   Usually followed by <Essay>.
   ============================================================ */
---

<div class="preface"><slot /></div>

<style>
  /* `div.` lifts this one step above the post body's own paragraph
     colour rule (.prose p / .fprose p), which would otherwise tie on
     specificity and win or lose on stylesheet order. Direct children only,
     so a nested component keeps its own colour. */
  div.preface > :global(:is(p, ul, ol)) {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  /* a loose list's <li><p> keeps the muted colour too */
  div.preface > :global(:is(ul, ol) p) {
    color: inherit;
  }
</style>
